! S.frr — Customer of A, peer of B, provider of C
!
! Relationships (Gao-Rexford):
!   Providers:  A (10.0.1.1)  — S pays A for upstream transit
!   Peers:      B (10.0.2.2)  — S and B exchange traffic settlement-free
!   Customers:  C (10.0.3.2)  — C pays S for transit
!
! Key economic incentive: C pays S, so S *prefers* routes learned from C
! (local-pref 300). When D's prefix is reachable via A (provider, cost money),
! B (peer, free), and C (customer, earns money), S will always choose the path
! through C — this is Gao-Rexford in action.
!
! Local preference (drives best-path selection):
!   300 = customer-learned  (C's routes — S earns revenue sending this way)
!   200 = peer-learned      (B's routes — settlement-free, neutral)
!   100 = provider-learned  (A's routes — S pays, use only as last resort)
!
! Export policy (valley-free routing):
!   → providers: own prefix + customer routes only (no re-exporting peer/provider)
!   → peers:     own prefix + customer routes only (no free transit for peers)
!   → customers: full table (C pays for global reachability)

bgp community-list standard CUSTOMER-ROUTES permit 65005:100
!
ip prefix-list OWN-PREFIX seq 5 permit 10.255.5.1/32
!
! Inbound from provider A: deprioritise (costs money)
route-map FROM-PROVIDER permit 10
 set community 65005:300
 set local-preference 100
!
! Inbound from peer B: neutral
route-map FROM-PEER permit 10
 set community 65005:200
 set local-preference 200
!
! Inbound from customer C: prioritise (earns money)
! This makes S route toward D via C rather than via A or B.
route-map FROM-CUSTOMER permit 10
 set community 65005:100
 set local-preference 300
!
! To provider/peer: only own prefix and customer (C's) routes.
! Re-exporting peer/provider routes would give away free transit.
route-map TO-PROVIDER permit 10
 match ip address prefix-list OWN-PREFIX
route-map TO-PROVIDER permit 20
 match community CUSTOMER-ROUTES
route-map TO-PROVIDER deny 30
!
route-map TO-PEER permit 10
 match ip address prefix-list OWN-PREFIX
route-map TO-PEER permit 20
 match community CUSTOMER-ROUTES
route-map TO-PEER deny 30
!
! To customer C: full table (C pays for global reachability).
route-map TO-CUSTOMER permit 10
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  ! Provider
  neighbor 10.0.1.1 route-map FROM-PROVIDER in
  neighbor 10.0.1.1 route-map TO-PROVIDER out
  ! Peer
  neighbor 10.0.2.2 route-map FROM-PEER in
  neighbor 10.0.2.2 route-map TO-PEER out
  ! Customer
  neighbor 10.0.3.2 route-map FROM-CUSTOMER in
  neighbor 10.0.3.2 route-map TO-CUSTOMER out
 exit-address-family
!
